      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1864, cattleman Stevens brought livestock into Williamson Valley, linking it to Prescott’s new markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://williamsonvalley.org/us/williamson-valley-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Thomas Simmons set up a stage station in the 1860s, making Williamson a key travel stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://williamsonvalley.org/us/williamson-valley-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Simmons named the station Wilson in 1871, then renamed it Williamson Valley in 1873.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://williamsonvalley.org/us/williamson-valley-history/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Williamson Museum chronicles the town’s mining past and its modern charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://arizonacityliving.com/city/williamson-az/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Williamson’s historic district preserves adobe buildings that echo the town’s early days.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
